<h3>4.1 Overall Architecture</h3>
<p>The system architecture follows a modern, scalable microservices approach:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Presentation Layer (Frontend):</strong>
<ul>
<li><em>Web App:</em> Developed using React.js or Next.js, providing complex dashboards, Gantt charts, and analytical interfaces.</li>
<li><em>Mobile App:</em> Developed using React Native for cross-platform (iOS/Android) compatibility, focusing on offline capabilities, camera integration, and simplified data entry for field workers.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Application Layer (Backend):</strong> Built on Node.js/Express or Python (FastAPI), acting as the API gateway. This layer handles business logic, authentication (OAuth 2.0, JWT), and routes requests to specific microservices (e.g., Document Service, AI Service, Scheduling Service).</li>
<li><strong>AI &amp; Analytics Engine:</strong> A dedicated Python-based processing environment hosting the Machine Learning models (using Scikit-Learn, TensorFlow/PyTorch) and NLP agents (leveraging APIs like OpenAI or open-source local LLMs).</li>
<li><strong>Data Layer:</strong>
<ul>
<li><em>Relational Database (PostgreSQL):</em> For structured transactional data (users, projects, financial ledgers).</li>
<li><em>NoSQL Database (MongoDB):</em> For flexible, unstructured data (logs, IoT sensor streams).</li>
<li><em>Object Storage (AWS S3/Azure Blob):</em> For documents, blueprints, and images.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p><img width="600" src="assets/coding_workflow.png" alt="Coding Workflow Flowchart">
<em>Figure 4: Coding and System Architecture Workflow of the NOVA Platform.</em></p>
<h3>4.2 Key System Modules</h3>
<h4>4.2.1 Core Project Management (The Foundation)</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Intelligent Scheduling &amp; Gantt:</strong> Moving beyond static CPM, this module allows dynamic scheduling. It integrates with the AI engine to suggest timeline adjustments based on resource availability.</li>
<li><strong>Document &amp; RFI Management:</strong> Centralized repository for all drawings, specs, and contracts.</li>
<li><strong>Financial &amp; Resource Tracking:</strong> Real-time monitoring of budget vs. actuals, labor hours, and material procurement.</li>
</ul>
<h4>4.2.2 AI-Assisted Decision Support Modules</h4>
<p>This is the primary differentiator of the platform.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Risk and Delay Predictor:</strong> Analyzes real-time inputs (e.g., delayed material delivery logged on mobile, adverse weather forecasts pulled via API) against historical patterns to flag potential delays. <em>Example UI: A traffic-light system on the project dashboard where &quot;Red&quot; indicates an AI-predicted 80% probability of a critical path delay within the next 14 days.</em></li>
<li><strong>Smart Document Assistant:</strong> Uses LLMs to allow users to query project data conversationally. <em>Example: A user types, &quot;What are the contractual penalties for a 2-week concrete delay?&quot; The system retrieves the exact clause from the 500-page contract PDF.</em></li>
</ul>
<h4>4.2.3 Sustainability and Green Business Dashboard</h4>
<p>To drive green business performance, sustainability is elevated to a primary project constraint alongside time, cost, and quality.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Dynamic Carbon Emission Calculator:</strong> Unlike static LCA, this tool calculates emissions dynamically. As a site manager logs the receipt of 100 tons of concrete from Supplier A, the system immediately calculates the embodied carbon based on Supplier A’s specific Environmental Product Declaration (EPD) database. It also tracks fuel usage of on-site machinery via IoT.</li>
<li><strong>Sustainability KPI Tracker:</strong> Monitors waste diversion rates, water usage, and local material sourcing percentages against project goals and green building certification requirements (e.g., LEED credits).</li>
<li><strong>Eco-Optimization Recommender:</strong> The AI suggests alternatives. For instance, if the schedule allows for a longer curing time, the system might recommend switching to a concrete mix with higher fly-ash content to significantly reduce the carbon footprint, presenting the trade-off between time and environmental impact to the project manager.</li>
</ul>
